            <ArticleTitle>[Relationship between methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase gene polymorphism and coronary heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>300-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This study inquired into the relationship between methylenetetrahydrofolate reductase (MTHFR) gene polymorphism and coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">By polymerase chain reaction and restriction fragment length polymorphism (PCR-RFLP), MTHFR 677C--&gt;T mutation was detected in 79 healthy controls and 69 patients with coronary heart disease.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The frequency of MTHFR variant V677 of patients was significantly higher than that of healthy controls (P&lt;0.01).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This study demonstrated that MTHFR gene V677 mutation was probably one of the genetic risk factors of coronary heart disease and this provided a new basis for exploring the relevant pathogenesis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
